  "body": "The following two things come up semi regularly:\r\n1. Synapse will include all events in the next transaction that have happened since the last transaction. This can lead to a scenario where we end up with large numbers of events in a single transaction, which the AS then takes a long time to process, causing the next transaction to also be very large, introducing large amounts of lag that the AS doesn't recover from. We should limit the number of events we bundle into a transaction.\r\n2. If the AS is marked down then for every event persisted we create a *new* transaction for that AS with a single event in it. When the AS comes back online Synapse will then send these transactions one at a time, which can mean that an AS can take a very very long time to catch up, even if its processing the events quickly. We should send transactions with multiple events instead (though not too many).",
